      "content": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "takeaways",
            "title": "Key takeaways",
            "items": [
              "Pass the summary, the steps already tried and the reason for the hand-off.",
              "Route by skill and urgency, not by whoever is free first."
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "h2",
            "text": "Why hand-offs lose the thread"
          },
          {
            "type": "p",
            "html": "Most repeat contacts start at a hand-off. The person who picks up the case sees a ticket, not the conversation, so the customer starts again. A good path carries <strong>what was checked</strong> and <em>why</em> it stopped."
          },
          {
            "type": "ul",
            "items": [
              "A two-line summary written for the next person",
              "The account checks that already passed",
              "The rule that triggered the hand-off"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "blockquote",
            "html": "Our leads read four lines and know exactly where to pick up.",
            "cite": "Support lead at a fictional lender"
          },
          {
            "type": "h2",
            "text": "Designing the route"
          },
          {
            "type": "p",
            "html": "Map each intent to a named queue and a time limit. Review the paths monthly with the <a href=\"/articles/support-metrics-that-matter\">metrics that matter</a> beside them."
          }
        ]
      },
      "motion": {
        "profile": "none",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "none"
      }
